Z||000000||Bigdaddyfiero||03-25-2001||07:06 PM||||87 Fiero GT v6,auto<BR>Just got the GT <P>egr solenoid - where does the hose connect to the throtle body.Yes I looked at the vac diag. , but cant find a open port around the throtle body. (It probably was disconected)<P>Back bumper support - are they the same for all years and models. (Need one for mine)<P>Are Fiero frames the same for all years and models.<P>Thanks for any help, I am new to the v6.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-25-2001||10:46 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bigdaddyfiero:<BR><B>87 Fiero GT v6,auto<BR>Just got the GT <P>egr solenoid - where does the hose connect to the throtle body.Yes I looked at the vac diag. , but cant find a open port around the throtle body. (It probably was disconected)<P>Back bumper support - are they the same for all years and models. (Need one for mine)<P>Are Fiero frames the same for all years and models.<P>Thanks for any help, I am new to the v6.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The ports on the TB are under it, one large on the linkage side. A small one under the IAC sensor. The V-6's use hard plastic lines to rubber 90* connections. Sometimes the hard plastic lines pull out of the rubber. Or the plastic lines split with age.<P>Bumper support for GT's I think is the same from 86 thru 88.<P>Frame/chassis is the same from 85 thru 87. I think the 84's are slightly different do to harness' are routed differently. 88's have a whole different suspension/cradle. The rear strut towers are angled differently and closer together. The cage area for the passenger compartment I think is the same.<BR>The front is different due to suspension. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bigdaddyfiero||03-25-2001||11:27 PM||||Thanks Oreif<BR>Ill ck out the erg tomorrow.<BR>The reason I asked about the frame is I have slight rear end damage where the bumper support bolts on, the pass. side i should be able to straighten out. The driver side maybe not, but I have a 84 se for parts for my 86 coup and I thought i might be able to cut 3 to 5 inches off it and weld it to the 87 gt.  ||||reg||10
